    "scenesThatPass": [
      "HEDDA: Who are you looking at?\nTHEA: No one.\nHEDDA: Everyone.\nTHEA: There’s this woman that Eileen used to be... acquainted with. She says she tried to shoot her when Eileen broke it off.",
      "JANE: Hedda, darling, let’s have music.\nHEDDA: What?\nJANE: What’s the matter with you? I thought this was going to be a rager. You seemed absolutely ready for carnage when you invited me.\nJANE: Music! Damn it, Hedda.",
      "EILEEN: I’ve brought a couple of friends if that’s all right?\nHEDDA: The more the merrier!",
      "EILEEN: And that’s all I wanted. So I put nothing remotely controversial in the book.\nHEDDA: Isn’t the book about sex?\nEILEEN: In the classical era. No one is scandalized by people fucking on millennia old clay pots. Or perhaps I’m mistaken. Anyway, the real book, th…\nEILEEN: The next book. Something of a sequel to the first.",
      "HEDDA: Where are you going?\nEILEEN: Where’s Thea? I’m tired of running around this ridiculous hedge. I’m back in town less than a day and I’m already wrapped up in your frivolo…"
    ]
  },
